{%- comment -%}
  Returns "true" or "false" for use with render + capture.

  A product is visible in a market unless every one of its variants is
  explicitly out of stock (per Phase A's live region metafields) for
  that market's warehouse(s). Unset metafields count as available
  (fail-open) — see
  docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-11-market-inventory-gating-phase-b-design.md.

  Non-shipping variants (requires_shipping == false — digital/subscription
  products like CastleFit) always count as available, regardless of the
  metafield value. Phase A's Flow workflows derive these metafields from
  real ShipBob per-warehouse stock, which isn't a meaningful signal for a
  product that's never fulfilled from a warehouse — gating on it hid a
  genuinely purchasable product. Found 2026-08-12: CastleFit was missing
  from the homepage Featured Products carousel because of this.

  Canada market: custom.in_stock_canada
  Europe/United Kingdom markets: custom.in_stock_eu_uk
  Other markets (default): custom.in_stock_us_row

  Optional: canada_market (boolean) — skip re-detecting market when already set via include
  Optional: eu_uk_market (boolean) — skip re-detecting market when already set via include
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign target_product = product -%}
{%- if target_product == blank -%}
  {%- assign target_product = check_product -%}
{%- endif -%}

{%- if canada_market == true -%}
  {%- assign is_canada_market = true -%}
{%- elsif canada_market == false -%}
  {%- assign is_canada_market = false -%}
{%- else -%}
  {%- capture is_canada_capture -%}
    {%- render 'market-is-canada' -%}
  {%- endcapture -%}
  {%- assign is_canada_capture = is_canada_capture | strip -%}
  {%- assign is_canada_market = false -%}
  {%- if is_canada_capture == 'true' -%}
    {%- assign is_canada_market = true -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}

{%- if eu_uk_market == true -%}
  {%- assign is_eu_uk_market = true -%}
{%- elsif eu_uk_market == false -%}
  {%- assign is_eu_uk_market = false -%}
{%- else -%}
  {%- capture is_eu_uk_capture -%}
    {%- render 'market-is-eu-uk' -%}
  {%- endcapture -%}
  {%- assign is_eu_uk_capture = is_eu_uk_capture | strip -%}
  {%- assign is_eu_uk_market = false -%}
  {%- if is_eu_uk_capture == 'true' -%}
    {%- assign is_eu_uk_market = true -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Region-based gating (Phase B, 2026-08-11): a product is visible unless
  EVERY one of its variants has the relevant region's in-stock metafield
  explicitly set to false. Unset (not yet backfilled by Phase A's Flow
  workflows) or true both keep it visible — fail-open, see
  docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-11-market-inventory-gating-phase-b-design.md §4.
  Non-shipping variants skip the metafield check entirely (see comment
  above) — they're always counted as available.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign any_variant_available = false -%}
{%- for variant in target_product.variants -%}
  {%- if variant.requires_shipping == false -%}
    {%- assign any_variant_available = true -%}
  {%- else -%}
    {%- if is_canada_market -%}
      {%- assign region_stock = variant.metafields.custom.in_stock_canada -%}
    {%- elsif is_eu_uk_market -%}
      {%- assign region_stock = variant.metafields.custom.in_stock_eu_uk -%}
    {%- else -%}
      {%- assign region_stock = variant.metafields.custom.in_stock_us_row -%}
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- unless region_stock == false -%}
      {%- assign any_variant_available = true -%}
    {%- endunless -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- if any_variant_available -%}true{%- else -%}false{%- endif -%}
